{"id": 3973176, "title": "CVE-2026-86410:  redirect to SFTP or SCP bypasses host verification", "submitted": "2026-08-27", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3973176", "excerpt": "## Summary\n\n`ssh_setopts()` in `src/config2setopts.c` returns immediately when the initial URL is not SCP or SFTP. This means `--knownhosts`, `--hostpubsha256`, and `--hostpubmd5` are never installed on the easy handle when the initial URL is HTTPS. If `--location --proto-redir +sftp` is used and the server returns a `Location: sftp://…` redirect, the SFTP connection proceeds without any of the user's requested SSH host-key verification.\n\nCommit `ab3bb8cd8be8f9d4acb97da0418abc279182041e` fixed CVE-2026-12064 for `--proto-default` but did not touch the early-return guard that causes this redirect variant. The vulnerable guard is present in the released `curl-8_21_0` tag and at current HEAD.\n\n## Affected versions\n\nAffected versions: curl CLI 7.81.0 through 8.21.0, plus affected 8.22.0\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `src/config2setopts.c`, `ssh_setopts()` (line 205) bails out early:\n\n```c\nif(use_proto != proto_scp && use_proto != proto_sftp)\n  return CURLE_OK;\n```\n\n`use_proto` is derived from the initial command-line URL in `config2setopts()`. When the initial URL is HTTPS, none of `CURLOPT_SSH_KNOWNHOSTS`, `CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_SHA256`, or `CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_MD5` are set on the easy handle. Redirect handling occurs inside libcurl and does not rerun `config2setopts()`, so the SFTP connection has no host-key verification policy. Verbose output on the redirected connection explicitly reports `SSH: no knownhosts file configured`.\n\n## Security impact\n\nAn attacker who can impersonate the redirected SFTP endpoint can substitute downloaded content while curl reports success. The user's explicit `--knownhosts` or `--hostpubsha256` policy is silently ignored.\n\nPreconditions:\n\n1. SSH-enabled curl build (libssh2 or libssh).\n2. `--location --proto-redir +sftp` (user explicitly enables SFTP redirects).\n3. A trusted HTTPS origin that redirects to SFTP.\n4. Authentication credentials usable at the SFTP endpoint.\n5. An attacker able to impersonate the SSH endpoint.\n\nI expect Low severity given the narrow attack surface and leave classification to the security team.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Build an affected curl command-line tool, starting with 7.81.0, with SFTP support through libssh2 or libssh and HTTPS support through a TLS backend.\n2. Start an SFTP server with a known SSH host key, valid test credentials, and a file containing recognizable test data.\n3. Create a `known_hos", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Confirmed by the code", "tone": "good", "explain": "The real code shows the flaw the report describes.", "confidence": 0.95, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "grounded", "rev": "b73a4f00b2a6", "rev_source": "master on 2026-08-27", "counts": {"grounded": 14, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 0}, "problems": []}, "summary": "Curl bypasses user-requested SSH host-key verification when redirecting from HTTPS to SFTP, ignoring --knownhosts and --hostpubsha256 settings.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "ssh_setopts() returns early when the initial URL is not SCP or SFTP, preventing SSH options from being set on the easy handle", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The function ssh_setopts() at line 205-258 contains the guard `if(use_proto != proto_scp && use_proto != proto_sftp) return CURLE_OK;` at lines 210-211, which prevents SSH host verification options from being installed when the initial URL protocol is not SCP or SFTP.", "citations": [{"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 210, "note": "Early return when use_proto is not proto_scp or proto_sftp", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 211, "note": "Returns CURLE_OK without setting any SSH options", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "src/config2setopts.c, line 205", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The report cites line 205; the function definition begins at line 205 in the provided source.", "citations": [{"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 205, "note": "Function definition of ssh_setopts starts here", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "initial URL is HTTPS, causing use_proto to exclude SCP/SFTP and skip host-key option installation", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "In config2setopts(), use_proto is determined from the initial command-line URL at line 1190 and passed to ssh_setopts() at line 955. When the initial URL is HTTPS, use_proto will be proto_http, causing the early return in ssh_setopts().", "citations": [{"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 1190, "note": "use_proto derived from initial URL via url_proto_and_rewrite", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 955, "note": "ssh_setopts called with use_proto from initial URL", "valid": false}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "When redirected to SFTP via --location --proto-redir, the SFTP connection proceeds without any SSH host-key verification, ignoring user-specified --knownhosts or --hostpubsha256", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "All three SSH host verification options (lines 219, 223-224, 241) are installed only after the early-return guard. When the initial URL is HTTPS, the guard triggers and none of these options are set on the easy handle. A subsequent redirect to SFTP (allowed by --proto-redir +sftp) will use the same easy handle without these options, so host-key verification is silently skipped.", "citations": [{"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 219, "note": "CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_MD5 set only after guard", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 223, "note": "CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_SHA256 set only after guard", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 241, "note": "CURLOPT_SSH_KNOWNHOSTS set only after guard", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "Use HTTPS server that redirects to SFTP, configure mismatching --knownhosts, and observe successful download despite verification policy", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The reproduction steps are plausible given the code structure: config2setopts() runs once per transfer using the initial URL's protocol; redirects are handled inside libcurl without re-running config2setopts(). The mismatching --knownhosts file would be ignored on the redirected SFTP connection because CURLOPT_SSH_KNOWNHOSTS was never set.", "citations": [{"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 210, "note": "Guard prevents SSH options for non-SSH initial URLs", "valid": true}, {"file": "src/config2setopts.c", "line": 955, "note": "ssh_setopts called once during initial setup, not on redirect", "valid": false}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://sourceware.org/pipermail/cygwin-announce/2025-November/012622.html", "title": "Updated: curl/libcurl-doc/-devel/4, mingw64-x86_64-curl 8.17 - multi-protocol file transfer tool", "for": "The fix requires removing the protocol guard in ssh_setopts() so SSH options are installed regardless of the initial URL protocol"}, {"url": "https://libssh2.org", "title": "libssh2", "for": "The fix requires removing the protocol guard in ssh_setopts() so SSH options are installed regardless of the initial URL protocol"}, {"url": "https://sourceware.org/pipermail/cygwin-announce/2026-January/012778.html", "title": "Updated: curl/libcurl-doc/-devel/4, mingw64-x86_64-curl 8.18 - multi-protocol file transfer tool", "for": "The fix requires removing the protocol guard in ssh_setopts() so SSH options are installed regardless of the initial URL protocol"}], "key_reasons": ["The early-return guard in ssh_setopts() (src/config2setopts.c:210-211) is present in both the current master and the curl-8_21_0 release, confirming the vulnerability exists in released versions.", "The guard prevents installation of CURLOPT_SSH_KNOWNHOSTS, CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_SHA256, and CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_MD5 when the initial URL is not SCP/SFTP.", "Redirect handling in libcurl does not re-run config2setopts(), so an HTTPS→SFTP redirect uses an easy handle that lacks the user's requested SSH host verification options.", "The user explicitly enables SFTP redirects (--proto-redir +sftp) and explicitly requests host verification (--knownhosts/--hostpubsha256); the bug silently drops the latter when the former is used.", "This is not API misuse, local attack, or documented behavior — it is an implementation oversight that bypasses a user-configured security policy."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and reproduction steps. The early-return guard in ssh_setopts() (src/config2setopts.c:210-211) does prevent SSH host-verification options from being installed when the initial URL is HTTPS, and those options are not re-applied when a redirect switches to SFTP. This silently ignores the user's --knownhosts/--hostpubsha256 policy. We will treat this as a valid security issue and prepare a fix that installs SSH options regardless of the initial protocol, since they are harmless on non-SSH transfers but required for redirected SSH transfers.", "code": [{"name": "src/config2setopts.c", "start": 180, "end": 258, "reason": "lines 205-205 cited by the report; definition of ssh_setopts", "rows": [{"n": 180, "text": "        result = ipfs_url_rewrite(uh, schemep, url, config);", "notes": []}, {"n": 181, "text": "        /* short-circuit proto_token, we know it is ipfs or ipns */", "notes": []}, {"n": 182, "text": "        if(curl_strequal(schemep, proto_ipfs))", "notes": []}, {"n": 183, "text": "          proto = proto_ipfs;", "notes": []}, {"n": 184, "text": "        else if(curl_strequal(schemep, proto_ipns))", "notes": []}, {"n": 185, "text": "          proto = proto_ipns;", "notes": []}, {"n": 186, "text": "        if(result)", "notes": []}, {"n": 187, "text": "          config->synthetic_error = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 188, "text": "      }", "notes": []}, {"n": 189, "text": "#endif /* !CURL_DISABLE_IPFS */", "notes": []}, {"n": 190, "text": "      if(uc == CURLUE_OUT_OF_MEMORY)", "notes": []}, {"n": 191, "text": "        result = CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 192, "text": "      curl_free(schemep);", "notes": []}, {"n": 193, "text": "    }", "notes": []}, {"n": 194, "text": "    else if(uc == CURLUE_OUT_OF_MEMORY)", "notes": []}, {"n": 195, "text": "      result = CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 196, "text": "    curl_url_cleanup(uh);", "notes": []}, {"n": 197, "text": "  }", "notes": []}, {"n": 198, "text": "  else", "notes": []}, {"n": 199, "text": "    result = CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 200, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 201, "text": "  *scheme = proto ? proto : \"?\"; /* Never match if not found. */", "notes": []}, {"n": 202, "text": "  return result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 203, "text": "}", "notes": []}, {"n": 204, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 205, "text": "static CURLcode ssh_setopts(struct OperationConfig *config, CURL *curl,", "notes": ["C2: Function definition of ssh_setopts starts here"]}, {"n": 206, "text": "                            const char *use_proto)", "notes": []}, {"n": 207, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 208, "text": "  CURLcode result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 209, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 210, "text": "  if(use_proto != proto_scp && use_proto != proto_sftp)", "notes": ["C1: Early return when use_proto is not proto_scp or proto_sftp", "C5: Guard prevents SSH options for non-SSH initial URLs"]}, {"n": 211, "text": "    return CURLE_OK;", "notes": ["C1: Returns CURLE_OK without setting any SSH options"]}, {"n": 212, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 213, "text": "  /* SSH and SSL private key uses same command-line option */", "notes": []}, {"n": 214, "text": "  MY_SETOPT_STR(curl, CURLOPT_SSH_PRIVATE_KEYFILE, config->key);", "notes": []}, {"n": 215, "text": "  MY_SETOPT_STR(curl, CURLOPT_SSH_PUBLIC_KEYFILE, config->pubkey);", "notes": []}, {"n": 216, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 217, "text": "  /* SSH host key md5 checking allows us to fail if we are not talking to who", "notes": []}, {"n": 218, "text": "     we think we should */", "notes": []}, {"n": 219, "text": "  MY_SETOPT_STR(curl, CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_MD5, config->hostpubmd5);", "notes": ["C4: CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_MD5 set only after guard"]}, {"n": 220, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 221, "text": "  /* SSH host key sha256 checking allows us to fail if we are not talking to", "notes": []}, {"n": 222, "text": "     who we think we should */", "notes": []}, {"n": 223, "text": "  MY_SETOPT_STR(curl, CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_SHA256,", "notes": ["C4: CURLOPT_SSH_HOST_PUBLIC_KEY_SHA256 set only after guard"]}, {"n": 224, "text": "                config->hostpubsha256);", "notes": []}, {"n": 225, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 226, "text": "  if(config->ssh_compression)", "notes": []}, {"n": 227, "text": "    my_setopt_long(curl, CURLOPT_SSH_COMPRESSION, 1);", "notes": []}, {"n": 228, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 229, "text": "  if(!config->insecure_ok) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 230, "text": "    char *known = config->knownhosts;", "notes": []}, {"n": 231, "text": "    if(!known) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 232, "text": "      char *found = findfile(\".ssh/known_hosts\", FALSE);", "notes": []}, {"n": 233, "text": "      if(found) {", "notes": []}, {"n": 234, "text": "        known = curlx_strdup(found);", "notes": []}, {"n": 235, "text": "        curl_free(found);", "notes": []}, {"n": 236, "text": "        if(!known)", "notes": []}, {"n": 237, "text": "          return CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;", "notes": []}, {"n": 238, "text": "      }", "notes": []}, {"n": 239, "text": "    }", "notes":